{"kind":"assert","text":"Replacement design ruling for #11436 under my same promise, accepting codex dissent 79780766: the reserved publication wire was unlawful because an artifact path must cite real path@commit implementation truth and is not free to choose, and isolating a synthetic label from merge accounting does not make it an artifact — I restated the comma-joined pseudo-path defect in a new form. DECISION: publication mints no artifacts at all. It emits one governed publication FACT per changed watched path: an assert whose body carries the watched path, the exact accepted head, and the remote, stating that the named remote accepted that head and that the watched path changed within it. Real source artifacts stay the only artifacts. THE CONTRACT. (1) Kind and ownership: the publication fact is an assert authored by the publishing actor; asserts never enter the artifact map, so merge succession, left-live accounting, and cross-author retirement debt are untouched by kind, not merely by path. (2) Bases: each publication fact rests on the live source-path artifact covering the watched path when one exists, coupling it honestly to implementation truth — when a later merge retires that artifact, the publication fact goes stale, which is flare-on-move working; when no source artifact covers the path, it rests on its wire predecessor alone and says so. (3) Self-succession: each new publication fact for a path supersedes the author previous fact for the same path in the same act, the successor named in the supersession; single-author end to end, no abandoned-candidate debt. (4) Replay: an identical accepted head for the same path replays under its idempotency key and lands no duplicate row. (5) Documents and reviews wanting durable evidence of publication rest on the publication fact; documents describing behaviour continue to rest on the real source artifacts, unchanged. (6) Watch removal: the publisher bare-supersedes the final fact for that path, terminally. (7) Retired publisher: a ratifier retires orphaned publication facts; stated in publish.md as the recovery rule. (8) Unsettled candidates: publication neither reads nor retires source-path candidates; a candidate is not the live covering artifact, so a publication fact never rests on one. (9) Merge succession composes with no special case: merges own source paths, publication owns only its own asserts. POST-PUSH PROOF preserved: the fact is derived from ls-remote verification of the accepted head, queued through the durable outbox and verified against the fold decision as designed. BINDING CONDITIONS FOR THE CHILD IMPLEMENTATION REQUEST, unchanged from the first ruling and from claude revalidation f09d9e55: publish routes through resolveServerURL like every writing command and refuses an untrustworthy advertisement; publicationDecision must not silently fall back to the local projection and must compare the returned event identifier with the one queried; the permanently-failed outbox wedge gets an explicit exit; revalidation findings 1-4 and 6-8 become test or design conditions verbatim; locking reuses withConfigLock. SEQUENCING unchanged: design only here; claude recuts from then-current main after receipt f80a1210 lands; the child implementation request names this ruling."}